{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And if there be a mishap.</b> According to the one who says [that] if he intended to kill this one and killed that one, he is liable — נפש תחת נפש means literally a life for a life. And according to the one who says he is exempt from death but liable monetarily, נפש תחת נפש is monetary, a ransom for his life. And according to Tanna of the school of Hezekiah, who holds in perek qamma of Bava Qamma that he is exempt even from money, the verse is expounded thus: ואם אסון יהיה — and he intended for the woman herself; ונתת נפש תחת נפש. And it is puzzling: what novelty is there in this, since he intended for the woman and is therefore killed? And to me it appears that one might have thought that since his intention was not carried out — for his primary intention was to kill the other person — he should not be liable; קמ\"ל [it comes to teach us]."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:45.070478646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}